rk1-speech contains no model weights, no compiled models and no code from the
projects below. Its installer downloads them from their own publishers, at the
versions pinned in versions.env, and runs them. They keep their own licences:

  moonshine-rknn (https://github.com/fursman/moonshine-rknn), MIT License:
    the speech recogniser. It runs Moonshine by Moonshine AI
    (https://github.com/moonshine-ai/moonshine, MIT License), moonshine-voice's
    model build, and Silero VAD (https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad, MIT).

  kokoro-rknn (https://github.com/fursman/kokoro-rknn), Apache License 2.0:
    the speech synthesiser. It runs Kokoro-82M by hexgrad
    (https://github.com/hexgrad/kokoro, Apache License 2.0) through kokoro-onnx
    by thewh1teagle (https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx, MIT License).
    Parts of kokoro-rknn's build/surgery.py are adapted from kokoro-server by
    marty1885 (https://github.com/marty1885/kokoro-server). kokoro-server had
    no licence file when kokoro-rknn was written; much of it derives from
    Kokoro, so kokoro-rknn treats what it adapted as carrying Kokoro's
    Apache License 2.0 terms (see kokoro-rknn's NOTICE). rk1-speech follows
    the same policy for anything it installs that derives from them.

  Rockchip's RKNN runtime (librknnrt) and rknn-toolkit2
    (https://github.com/airockchip/rknn-toolkit2): the NPU runtime and the
    graph compiler, under Rockchip's terms. The installer downloads
    librknnrt.so 2.5.0 from that repository and checks its sha256.

known-good/kokoro-rknn-buckets.sha256 lists only SHA-256 hashes of NPU graphs
compiled from Kokoro-82M; the graphs themselves are not distributed here.
